# Machine-local configuration for scripts/system-one and hooks/system-one-*.sh.
# Copy to ${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-~/.claude}/system-one.local.sh and fill it in.
# Never committed: it names a path on one machine. Plain shell assignments only;
# both the zsh wrapper and the bash hooks source it. An environment variable of
# the same name overrides the value here.

# Required for SYSTEM_ONE_BACKEND=laya (the default). The uv venv that holds
# laya-serve (the design created it at ~/.local/share/system-one/venv; any
# path works). The kev backend does not need it.
SYSTEM_ONE_VENV="$HOME/.local/share/system-one/venv"

# Loopback port the server listens on. Default 7811.
#SYSTEM_ONE_PORT=7811

# Minutes without a request before the watchdog stops the server. Default 30.
#SYSTEM_ONE_IDLE_MINUTES=30

# shadow: hooks only log what they would have done (default).
# show: identical to shadow (hooks never emit a permission decision); the
# distinct name lets `system-one status`, the statusline and the Agent Bar
# Hopping app say the user has opted in to seeing verdicts (shadow plus the
# status line row).
# act: hooks may emit a permission decision. The Bash hook only ever emits
# "ask" (never deny, since the deterministic guards already own hard blocks);
# the AskUserQuestion pre-check (system-one-ask.sh) is the one hook that
# denies, and only when the fired question is not naming_or_irreversible (a
# naming or hard-to-reverse ask is always legitimate and is never denied).
# Flip per the evaluation plan in the design doc, on the user's word only.
#SYSTEM_ONE_MODE=shadow

# Per-hook overrides of SYSTEM_ONE_MODE above (same three values). Unset means
# "use SYSTEM_ONE_MODE". Set these to try one hook in act mode without moving
# the others.
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_MODE=shadow
#SYSTEM_ONE_PROMPT_MODE=shadow
#SYSTEM_ONE_STOP_MODE=shadow
#SYSTEM_ONE_ASK_MODE=shadow

# Prompt hook only: the top kind probability act mode requires before it adds
# additionalContext (question/wish/correction only; order and other never get
# a line, nor does a slash command or a prompt under 3 words). Default 0.60,
# falling back to hooks/system-one-prompt-questions.json's "act_min" when
# unset here (see that file's "_act_min_comment" for why: prompt/kind is a
# choice question, so full-v1/eval.json's thresholds map carries no swept
# value for it, only per-class recall at argmax -- section 13 of the design
# doc).
# Measured on full-v1's test split (n=66) at 0.60, precision of the emitted
# line per class: question 0.90 (10 fired, 1 wrong), wish 1.00 (10 fired),
# correction 1.00 (14 fired); order/other never emit. No class is below 0.5,
# so there is no per-class floor.
#SYSTEM_ONE_PROMPT_ACT_MIN=0.60

# Prompt hook only: the delegate question's probability act mode requires
# before it adds the "hand this to a Sonnet or Haiku subagent" line (only for
# typed prompts of at least 8 words; never a slash command or a relayed
# message). Default 0.5, falling back to hooks/system-one-prompt-questions.json's
# "delegate.min". On full-v3's test split precision is 1.00 at 0.5 through 0.7
# (recall 0.30 to 0.27); the checkpoint's own swept threshold (0.159) would
# fire three times as often with a third of the lines wrong.
#SYSTEM_ONE_PROMPT_DELEGATE_MIN=0.5

# Fallback threshold for a hooks/system-one-bash.sh gate question that has no
# threshold in hooks/system-one-bash-questions.json. Default 0.70.
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_ASK=0.70

# Per-question overrides of the thresholds in hooks/system-one-bash-questions.json
# (the file's values come from the sweep in section 3.1 of
# notebook/2026-09-24-system-one-decision-model-integration.md; set one here
# only to depart from them).
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_ASK_FOREIGN_PROCESS=0.85
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_ASK_IRREVERSIBLE=0.75
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_ASK_LEAVES_MACHINE=0.60
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_ASK_NETWORK_INSTALL=0.50

# Where the pid files, server log and shadow.jsonl live.
# Default ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/system-one.
#SYSTEM_ONE_STATE_DIR="$HOME/.local/state/system-one"

# Which server `start` launches: laya (default) or kev. Both speak the same
# /v1/systemone wire shape, so `ask` and every hook work unchanged either way.
# Changing this while a server runs takes effect after `system-one stop`;
# `start` leaves a running server of the other shape alone and says so.
# Every shape starts with HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1: a start never downloads a model,
# so the checkpoint must already be on disk or in the Hugging Face cache.
#SYSTEM_ONE_BACKEND=laya

# laya backend only, optional. A fine-tuned Laya checkpoint directory (one
# that holds rl_agent_config.json and model.safetensors, loadable with
# laya.Agent(dir)), served side by side with the published "english" bundle
# via scripts/system-one-serve.py instead of laya-serve -- both preloaded
# (Router max_loaded=2). Unset serves only the published convaiinnovations/laya
# bundle, as "english" (SYSTEM_ONE_VENV/bin/laya-serve).
#SYSTEM_ONE_MODEL_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/system-one/models/full-v1"

# The name the checkpoint above is served and asked for under: a request's
# "model" field, `system-one ask --model`, the shadow-log model field and
# /health's loaded list all use it as is. Default: SYSTEM_ONE_MODEL_DIR's
# basename (e.g. "full-v1"). Lowercase [a-z0-9._-], and never one of laya's
# own names (english, multilingual, typed-decisions or an alias); `start`
# refuses anything else.
#SYSTEM_ONE_MODEL_NAME=full-v1

# Which model each hook asks (default english for all four). Set one to
# SYSTEM_ONE_MODEL_NAME's value to point that hook at the checkpoint instead
# of the published bundle. The stop hook asks both its questions
# (needless_table, overlong) in one call, so SYSTEM_ONE_STOP_MODEL covers
# both -- see hooks/system-one-stop.sh.
#SYSTEM_ONE_BASH_MODEL=english
#SYSTEM_ONE_PROMPT_MODEL=english
#SYSTEM_ONE_STOP_MODEL=english
#SYSTEM_ONE_ASK_MODEL=english

# Required when SYSTEM_ONE_BACKEND=kev. The kev checkout, with its own .venv
# already synced (started as `cd <dir> && uv run --offline --extra serve
# python -m kev.serve`; uv must be on PATH).
#SYSTEM_ONE_KEV_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/system-one/kev"

# kev backend only. Passed as kev.serve's --run: a Hugging Face id
# (owner/name, optionally @revision; must already be in the HF cache) or a
# run directory holding head.pt, relative to the checkout or absolute.
# Default jaredpalmer/kev-0.8b.
#SYSTEM_ONE_KEV_MODEL=jaredpalmer/kev-0.8b
